    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d371">

                <pb facs="0668" n="536" sameAs="frus:frus1926v01/pg536"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.2315/306: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Morgan</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-07-14T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 14, 1926—5
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>38. I have discussed the matter of the treaty with Dr. Salomón, former Minister
                    for Foreign Affairs of Peru, who is in Washington at <pb facs="0669" n="537"
                        xml:id="pg537"/> present in connection with Tacna-Arica.<anchor n="66"
                        xml:id="d371-f1"/> He has communicated with President Leguía by cable and
                    informs me that the President has cabled in reply that as soon as Congress
                    convenes the end of this month he will again urge ratification of the treaty. I
                    think it would be helpful if Brazil would also make known to President Leguía
                    desire that treaty be ratified. You will keep the Department informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
